      "page_title": "Where to Put the Token",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Q: Cookie chosen — now CSRF?",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "What pairs with a cookie to stop CSRF?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "==Double-submit token==: same random value in cookie + header, server compares",
            "Check ==Origin== / `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin` on writes",
            "Require a ==custom header== (`X-CSRF: 1`) — forms can't set one, so preflight blocks it",
            "Apply on every **state-changing** call, not GETs"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "if (req.headers.origin !==",
            "    'https://app.io') return 403;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "*needs SameSite + CSRF token. Complexity climbs down the table: localStorage trivial, ==BFF== highest — and best.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Q: What shape today?",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Recommended storage for a 2026 SPA?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "==BFF (Backend-for-Frontend)==: browser holds **only** a session cookie",
            "Server keeps access + refresh tokens, attaches them server-side",
            "Middle ground: access token in a ==JS variable==, refresh in HttpOnly cookie",
            "Cost: page reload drops the var — needs a ==silent refresh== on boot"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "Browser -[sid cookie]-> BFF",
            "BFF -[Bearer eyJ..]-> API"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "iOS",
                "lines": [],
                "text": "==Keychain== for tokens; `ASWebAuthenticationSession` for login",
