    {
      "page_title": "Header & Key Resolution Attacks",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Leaks that need no attacker",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**Never log tokens** — scrub `Authorization` from access logs",
            "Redact it in APM traces, Sentry breadcrumbs, HAR dumps",
            "Mistake: `?token=eyJ...` in a download link or email",
            "URL tokens land in ==server logs==, ==history==, `Referer` — forever",
            "Send the token in the header; sign a short one-time URL instead"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Header Attacks",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why must `alg` be pinned server-side?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "==alg: none== accepted, signature segment empty, token trusted",
            "Algorithm read from the **attacker-controlled** header, not from config",
            "{red:RS256 to HS256}: public key fed to an HMAC verifier as the secret",
            "Anyone with the published JWKS can then mint `role: admin`"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "{\"alg\":\"none\",\"typ\":\"JWT\"}",
            "hdr.payload.        // empty sig",
            "hmac(pubKeyPEM, signingInput)",
            "// verifier forges its own tokens"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Key Resolution",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "How does `kid` handling get abused?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`kid` ignored, server tries __every key__ until one verifies",
            "`kid` used as a file path or SQL value, so it becomes injection",
            "{red:jku}/{red:x5u} fetched from a URL inside the token itself",
            "Attacker hosts a JWKS, signs with its own key, server obliges"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "keys.find(k => k.kid === kid)",
            "// NOT: keys.some(k => verify(k))",
            "allowedJku = ['iss.example.com']"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mistake",
            "Effect",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`alg` from header",
              "Forgery",
              "Pin list"
            ],
            [
              "Public key as HMAC",
              "Anyone signs",
              "Split verifiers"
            ],
            [
              "`decode` not `verify`",
              "Full bypass",
              "Verify first"
            ],
            [
              "Weak/shared secret",
              "Offline crack",
              "256-bit, per-env"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Component",
            "Holds",
            "Trusts"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Browser",
              "session cookie",
              "BFF"
            ],
            [
              "BFF",
              "access+refresh",
              "AS"
            ],
            [
              "Gateway",
              "JWKS cache",
              "`iss` sig"
            ],
            [
