      "page_title": "End-to-End Topology & Trade-offs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The End-to-End Picture",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Who holds which token?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "==SPA==: nothing but an `HttpOnly` session cookie",
            "==BFF==: access + refresh tokens, server-side store",
            "==Gateway==: verifies signature, forwards identity",
            "==Services==: re-check `aud`, never store tokens"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "SPA  --cookie-->  BFF",
            "BFF  --code+PKCE-->  AS",
            "BFF  --Bearer-->  Gateway",
            "Gateway --X-Sub/X-Scope--> svc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Internal service still checks ==`aud`== = its own id",
            "Defense in depth: mesh mTLS, not header trust alone",
            "**Never** forward user token blindly to peer service",
            "Peer calls: `client_credentials` or ==token exchange== (RFC 8693)"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Observability + Migration",
